  "tls_fixture_diagnosis": {
    "before_job": "7eadf3cc294d",
    "after_job": "f955e292dc8e",
    "before": "Standalone Node22 and the instrumented actual packaged Node24 process both loaded exactly one owned CA with the correct file hash, but its X509Certificate.ca was false and both fetches failed with UNABLE_TO_VERIFY_LEAF_SIGNATURE.",
    "correction": "Use owned explicit OpenSSL configurations and named root/server extension sections, then verify CA status, issuer/signatures, IP SAN, validity and sslserver purpose before listening. Existing host configuration also supplied CA constraints; exact duplicate-extension causation was not established from retained DER.",
    "after": "The generated root reports ca=true; Node22 and the same unchanged actual packaged ASAR return the default-deny HTTP404 when trusting the owned CA, while the no-CA control still rejects TLS.",
    "qualification": "Inspector observations are diagnostics, not public-preload packaged transport acceptance. The later complete bundle gate must independently establish that acceptance."
  },
  "implementation": [
    "Prefer the native bridge for workflow HTTP and SSE whenever it is available. Do not fall back to renderer networking after a native failure; retain browser/legacy compatibility when the namespace is absent.",
    "Admit only supported workflow routes and methods, safe encoded legacy IDs, bounded JSON bodies and non-nil operation UUIDs. Preserve the three existing connector workflow consumers.",
    "Read native URL, key and opaque revision; reject mismatched revisions and redirects before exposing responses or events. Retain authenticated Bearer/ApiKey fallback, bounded response/frame/chunk reads and stream_error handling.",
    "Require the current desktop window, top-level frame and approved renderer source; isolate operation IDs and cancellation by sender object. Bound per-owner active operations and abort work on connection invalidation, renderer replacement/crash/destruction or disposal.",
    "Cancel renderer operations and ignore late results across URL/key/revision/generation/organization changes, including A-to-B-to-A transitions. Release subscriptions and event listeners without allowing an older completion to affect another operation.",
    "Detach the preload event listener immediately at native EOF, including when an asynchronous event callback remains pending. Continue observing callback promises and report their errors. This cleanup refinement was identified in source review; no separate pre-fix failing runtime baseline was run.",
    "Replace renderer-only workflow interception with owned deny-by-default HTTP servers in native recovery/settings cases. Observe actual health API settlement and server-side traffic rather than waiting for a renderer response that native fetch bypasses.",
    "Issue owned root/server certificates with explicit extensions and validate their CA constraints, issuer/signatures, IP SAN, validity and sslserver purpose before the HTTPS fixture listens.",
    "Exercise real packaged HTTPS requests, TLS rejection without the owned CA, scoped trust with it, enforced renderer CSP, SSE cursors/UTF-8 decoding/cancellation and stale-revision rejection with no extra HTTP traffic.",
    "Retain packaged transport receipts and Linux Playwright reports in both CI workflows. Include bounded startup stderr in harness launch failures so missing native dependencies are diagnosable."
  ],
